{"vid":"mxITDEx1_1U","source":"mxITDEx1_1U.en.json3","lang":"en","cues":[{"t":0,"txt":"Stop mispronouncing these words in"},{"t":3.5,"txt":"English. They all have silent letters."},{"t":7.8,"txt":"You can't work this out on your own."},{"t":9.8,"txt":"Someone has to teach you, and that's why"},{"t":12.4,"txt":"I'm here today. And if your goal is to"},{"t":15,"txt":"speak English with a clear, natural"},{"t":18.4,"txt":"British accent, my 5-day British accent"},{"t":22.2,"txt":"boot camp is exactly what you need. It's"},{"t":25,"txt":"a short but complete, targeted training"},{"t":28.2,"txt":"program with daily practice routines, so"},{"t":31.2,"txt":"you can see real improvements from day"},{"t":33.5,"txt":"one. And right now, you can join for a"},{"t":35.8,"txt":"special discounted price. To learn more"},{"t":39.1,"txt":"and join, click the link in the"},{"t":41.2,"txt":"description box or scan the QR code"},{"t":43.9,"txt":"there. Okay, let's get started with the"},{"t":46.4,"txt":"lesson. I'm going to show you a pair of"},{"t":49.4,"txt":"words which both have the same silent"},{"t":52.9,"txt":"letter. Say the words out loud and try"},{"t":56.4,"txt":"to identify the silent letter. Then,"},{"t":59.2,"txt":"listen and repeat after me to check and"},{"t":61.8,"txt":"practice. Here's our first pair. Try it"},{"t":64.6,"txt":"yourself."},{"t":68.6,"txt":"Listen and repeat after me."},{"t":71.5,"txt":"handsome"},{"t":73.7,"txt":"Wednesday"},{"t":75.6,"txt":"Now, in both of these words, the letter"},{"t":77.8,"txt":"D is silent. It's not handsome or"},{"t":82.8,"txt":"Wednesday."},{"t":84.6,"txt":"Drop the duh sound. handsome Wednesday"},{"t":89.5,"txt":"Can you think of any more words with a"},{"t":91.1,"txt":"silent D? Sandwich and handkerchief are"},{"t":94.8,"txt":"two common examples, although some"},{"t":96.9,"txt":"people do say \"sandwich\"."},{"t":99.7,"txt":"I think it's harder to pronounce that"},{"t":101.2,"txt":"way. Another common pronunciation I like"},{"t":103.7,"txt":"is actually with a \"m\" sound, \"samwich\"."},{"t":107.6,"txt":"Okay, our second pair of words. Say them"},{"t":110.4,"txt":"out loud now. Can you spot the silent"},{"t":112.7,"txt":"letter?"},{"t":114.2,"txt":"Okay, listen and repeat."},{"t":117,"txt":"biscuit"},{"t":119.5,"txt":"circuit"},{"t":122.3,"txt":"So, both of these words have a silent U."},{"t":125.8,"txt":"It's not bisquit or circuit. biscuit,"},{"t":129.7,"txt":"circuit. This silent U confuses my"},{"t":132.5,"txt":"students in other common words like"},{"t":134.7,"txt":"build and builder. So, take care with"},{"t":138,"txt":"those words, too."},{"t":140,"txt":"Okay, pair number three. Which letter is"},{"t":142.5,"txt":"silent in both of these words? Read them"},{"t":145.2,"txt":"aloud. See what you think."},{"t":147.3,"txt":"The letter H is silent. Listen and"},{"t":150.2,"txt":"repeat."},{"t":151.8,"txt":"honest"},{"t":154.2,"txt":"heir"},{"t":155.7,"txt":"We don't say honest or hair. Drop the h"},{"t":160.8,"txt":"sound. Can you think of any other words"},{"t":163.3,"txt":"beginning with a silent H? H itself"},{"t":167.4,"txt":"shouldn't have the h sound at the"},{"t":169.5,"txt":"beginning. H."},{"t":171.5,"txt":"There's also hour,"},{"t":173.5,"txt":"honor,"},{"t":174.7,"txt":"and"},{"t":175.8,"txt":"herb."},{"t":177.5,"txt":"In British English, we say herb. Herb is"},{"t":181.4,"txt":"more North American pronunciation. I say"},{"t":184.2,"txt":"herb. Americans tend to say herb. Now,"},{"t":188,"txt":"be careful with your article usage with"},{"t":190.1,"txt":"these silent H words. We need to use an,"},{"t":194,"txt":"not a, as they begin with vowel sounds."},{"t":197.9,"txt":"It was an honest mistake."},{"t":200.6,"txt":"Give me an hour. There are lots more"},{"t":203.3,"txt":"silent H words in English, but most of"},{"t":205.7,"txt":"them are so common, they usually don't"},{"t":208.2,"txt":"cause confusion. The letters WH in what,"},{"t":212.8,"txt":"where, when, and why, for example, are"},{"t":215.5,"txt":"just pronounced with a w sound. My"},{"t":217.7,"txt":"students do sometimes get confused by"},{"t":220.1,"txt":"the pronunciation of the letters CH in"},{"t":223.6,"txt":"some of these words, though. Look at"},{"t":225.5,"txt":"these four words."},{"t":227.5,"txt":"How are the letters CH pronounced in"},{"t":230.2,"txt":"each one? Well, in the first word,"},{"t":232.9,"txt":"chaos, the letters c h make a k sound,"},{"t":237.2,"txt":"like in school, scheme, mechanic, and"},{"t":241.4,"txt":"chemistry. Notice it's not chemistry,"},{"t":244.6,"txt":"it's chemistry."},{"t":247,"txt":"Now, in chore, the c h is pronounced ch,"},{"t":250.9,"txt":"like in church and choose."},{"t":254.3,"txt":"But, the c h in chef is pronounced sh."},{"t":260.3,"txt":"But, in yacht, the letters c h are"},{"t":264,"txt":"silent. Don't get caught out by those"},{"t":267,"txt":"sneaky silent letters. Time for pair"},{"t":269.6,"txt":"number four. Read these aloud."},{"t":273.6,"txt":"Now, you won't believe the number of"},{"t":275.6,"txt":"times I've heard students say, \"answer\""},{"t":279,"txt":"and \"sward\". But, these pronunciations"},{"t":282.1,"txt":"are not correct. Never pronounce the"},{"t":285.1,"txt":"letter w in these words. Instead, say,"},{"t":289.1,"txt":"\"answer\"."},{"t":290.4,"txt":"\"sward\"."},{"t":292,"txt":"You might have already noticed that the"},{"t":293.9,"txt":"letter w is silent when written with r"},{"t":298,"txt":"at the beginning of a word, like in"},{"t":301.1,"txt":"write,"},{"t":302.5,"txt":"wrist,"},{"t":304.2,"txt":"wrinkle, and wrong. Take care with those"},{"t":308.5,"txt":"silent w's."},{"t":310.6,"txt":"Similarly, the letter k is silent when"},{"t":313.4,"txt":"it appears with the letter n at the"},{"t":316.1,"txt":"beginning of a word. But, you"},{"t":318.9,"txt":"knew that, right? Knew. Can you think of"},{"t":322.6,"txt":"any other examples?"},{"t":325,"txt":"Well, we've got words like knife,"},{"t":329.1,"txt":"knuckle,"},{"t":331.3,"txt":"knight,"},{"t":333.3,"txt":"knee,"},{"t":335.4,"txt":"knit,"},{"t":336.9,"txt":"and knot, to name but a few. Okay, are"},{"t":341.3,"txt":"you ready for our fifth pair?"},{"t":343.7,"txt":"Here it is. Which letter is silent in"},{"t":347.1,"txt":"both of these words?"},{"t":349.3,"txt":"scissors"},{"t":351.6,"txt":"muscle"},{"t":353.2,"txt":"The letter C isn't pronounced in either"},{"t":356.1,"txt":"of these words."},{"t":358,"txt":"I hear skizzers and muscles all the"},{"t":361.6,"txt":"time. Drop the C and say scissors,"},{"t":365.4,"txt":"muscles instead. The letter C is silent"},{"t":368.6,"txt":"in a lot of words with the letters SC"},{"t":371.5,"txt":"together. Can you think of any more"},{"t":373.8,"txt":"examples?"},{"t":375.8,"txt":"Well, take care with the words scent,"},{"t":379.7,"txt":"scenario,"},{"t":381.7,"txt":"fascinate,"},{"t":383.5,"txt":"and ascent as they all have a silent C."},{"t":388.2,"txt":"Now, can you spot the silent letters in"},{"t":390.5,"txt":"pair number six? Both of these words"},{"t":393.4,"txt":"contain a silent F."},{"t":396.7,"txt":"Just joking. I'm just making sure you're"},{"t":398.1,"txt":"paying attention. It's the L that is"},{"t":400.4,"txt":"silent. I hear a lot of students trying"},{"t":403,"txt":"to pronounce the L. half, calf"},{"t":406.9,"txt":"Forget the all sound and just make the"},{"t":409.7,"txt":"long ah vowel sound instead."},{"t":412.7,"txt":"half"},{"t":414.2,"txt":"calf Much easier."},{"t":417.7,"txt":"Okay, pair number seven. Say these words"},{"t":419.9,"txt":"out loud. The letter S is silent in both"},{"t":422.9,"txt":"of these words."},{"t":424.6,"txt":"Isle is pronounced the same as the"},{"t":427,"txt":"contraction of I will and is one"},{"t":429.8,"txt":"syllable."},{"t":430.9,"txt":"isle"},{"t":432.7,"txt":"And it's not island, it's"},{"t":436,"txt":"island. Okay, time for our penultimate"},{"t":438.6,"txt":"pair. Read them aloud. Which letter is"},{"t":440.7,"txt":"silent? That's right. We never pronounce"},{"t":443.2,"txt":"the letter P at the beginning of words"},{"t":445.9,"txt":"with S. psychology"},{"t":449.5,"txt":"psychic"},{"t":451.9,"txt":"Can you think of any more words like"},{"t":453.4,"txt":"this?"},{"t":454.9,"txt":"Well, we've got psalm,"},{"t":457.3,"txt":"pseudonym,"},{"t":459.1,"txt":"and psychedelic. These are all words of"},{"t":462.1,"txt":"Greek origin."},{"t":464.4,"txt":"Oh, and take care with these silent P"},{"t":466.8,"txt":"words my students always mispronounce."},{"t":469.3,"txt":"We have cupboard and receipt. I know"},{"t":473.6,"txt":"it's so tempting to say receipt. receipt"},{"t":477.4,"txt":"cupboard receipt"},{"t":479.6,"txt":"Okay, time for our final pair."},{"t":482,"txt":"Read these words out loud and try to"},{"t":485,"txt":"identify the silent letter."},{"t":487.7,"txt":"Now, if you said musically or basically"},{"t":491.7,"txt":"with A or ah, try again. Musically."},{"t":496.9,"txt":"Basically."},{"t":498.7,"txt":"That's right. With some adverbs ending c"},{"t":501.5,"txt":"a l l y, the A is silent."},{"t":505.1,"txt":"Some speakers will pronounce it as a"},{"t":507.9,"txt":"soft schwa sound, musically, basically."},{"t":512.5,"txt":"This is less common. Most speakers don't"},{"t":515.3,"txt":"pronounce the letter A at all and just"},{"t":517.6,"txt":"say musically,"},{"t":519.7,"txt":"basically, both with just three"},{"t":522,"txt":"syllables. Right, we've got just enough"},{"t":524.3,"txt":"time for a quick shadowing task to help"},{"t":527,"txt":"you remember some of the words with"},{"t":528.8,"txt":"silent letters that we've covered today."},{"t":531.6,"txt":"I'll mark the silent letters on screen"},{"t":533.5,"txt":"to help you."},{"t":534.8,"txt":"Shadow me if you can or listen, pause"},{"t":538.8,"txt":"and then repeat."},{"t":540.4,"txt":"You ready? The handsome builder is"},{"t":543.4,"txt":"coming to put up the kitchen cupboards"},{"t":547.2,"txt":"at 5:30 this Wednesday. He's also going"},{"t":551.7,"txt":"to fit an island where I can keep my"},{"t":554.8,"txt":"knives,"},{"t":556.3,"txt":"scissors, receipts,"},{"t":559.6,"txt":"sandwich and biscuit tins, and basically"},{"t":563.6,"txt":"all of my bits and pieces. Honestly,"},{"t":567.6,"txt":"it's the best case scenario as I haven't"},{"t":571.5,"txt":"got the muscle to do it myself. How did"},{"t":574.9,"txt":"you find that? Rewind and speak along"},{"t":577.8,"txt":"with me again to practice further."},{"t":580.2,"txt":"Right, that brings us to the end of"},{"t":582.4,"txt":"today's video. Were there any silent"},{"t":584.6,"txt":"letters that surprised you?"},{"t":586.8,"txt":"Were there any that you think I should"},{"t":588.5,"txt":"have mentioned and didn't? Let me know"},{"t":590.9,"txt":"in the comments."},{"t":592.4,"txt":"And if you would like more help with"},{"t":593.9,"txt":"your British pronunciation, my 5-day"},{"t":596.8,"txt":"British Accent Bootcamp is on sale."},{"t":600,"txt":"Click on the link in the description box"},{"t":602,"txt":"or scan the QR code there to learn more"},{"t":604.7,"txt":"and join."},{"t":606,"txt":"I will see you in the next video. Bye."}],"words":[{"t":0,"w":"Stop"},{"t":1,"w":"mispronouncing"},{"t":2.32,"w":"these"},{"t":2.68,"w":"words"},{"t":3.4,"w":"in"},{"t":3.52,"w":"English."},{"t":4.6,"w":"They"},{"t":5,"w":"all"},{"t":5.64,"w":"have"},{"t":5.96,"w":"silent"},{"t":6.8,"w":"letters."},{"t":7.84,"w":"You"},{"t":8,"w":"can't"},{"t":8.4,"w":"work"},{"t":8.64,"w":"this"},{"t":8.88,"w":"out"},{"t":9.12,"w":"on"},{"t":9.24,"w":"your"},{"t":9.48,"w":"own."},{"t":9.8,"w":"Someone"},{"t":10.56,"w":"has"},{"t":10.92,"w":"to"},{"t":11.04,"w":"teach"},{"t":11.44,"w":"you,"},{"t":11.6,"w":"and"},{"t":11.8,"w":"that's"},{"t":12.12,"w":"why"},{"t":12.36,"w":"I'm"},{"t":12.56,"w":"here"},{"t":12.8,"w":"today."},{"t":13.44,"w":"And"},{"t":13.76,"w":"if"},{"t":14,"w":"your"},{"t":14.2,"w":"goal"},{"t":14.64,"w":"is"},{"t":14.88,"w":"to"},{"t":15.04,"w":"s